    description: "EVIDENCE (2026-09-25): packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/view_template_django.py defines `_CBV_TEMPLATE_NAME_BASES` (~L69-87). grep over packages/ finds no reader.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: DjangoCBVDefaultStrategy matches a class's base name against `_CBV_DEFAULT_SUFFIXES` with no path filter (~L336-351). `_template_name_sites` accepts `template_name` on ANY class, with no base check (~L299-320). A frozenset of CBV base names that nothing reads looks like a base-class gate that was designed and never wired. That is the \"value with no consumer\" shape.\n\nPRIOR ART: none found. WI-furap (wont_do) concerns the Rails path convention in the view-template linker, not Django.\n\nASKED: read the git history of the constant (git log -S). Then either wire it as the gate on `template_name` sites (measure edges before and after on a Django corpus repo; this may be a precision gain) or delete it and say why."  # d15b
